#. ~ Description of variant "5.56x45mm Mini Draco" of gun "ZPAP 85"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"A Serbian-made AK pattern rifle made by Zastava in 5.56x45mm NATO.  To avoid"
" import restrictions, Zastava USA has added a number of American-made parts."
"  This one is shorter and without a stock"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid "bolt-action hunting rifle"
msgid_plural "bolt-action hunting rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid ""
"Featuring a handsome set of wooden furnishings, a classic design, and a no "
"nonsense .270 caliber chambering, this is a powerful hunting rifle.  With a "
"tried and proven pedigree dating back over 60 years, millions of such rugged"
" arms have been made, exported, and used throughout the United States and "
"the world at large.  Where hunting is concerned, this is a highly capable "
"and well proven weapon in all respects.  Fortunate, given that your prey in "
"these dark days may turn out to be a little bit more feisty than typical "
"White-Tailed deer, moose, and black bears."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[0] "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[1] "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[2] "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[3] "Remington 700 .270 Win"

#. ~ Description of variant "bolt-action hunting rifle" of gun "Remington 700
#. .270 Win"
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid ""
"A classic bolt-action rifle chambered for .270 Winchester, very popular "
"among hunters.  This is a CDL SF model with a forged, fluted, 416 stainless "
"steel barrel threaded into the receiver and a recessed bolt face.  It has "
"checkered walnut furniture and a recoil pad to reduce perceived recoil."
msgstr ""
"Klasyczny karabin powtarzalny z komorą na nabój .270 Winchester, bardzo "
"popularny wśród myśliwych. Jest to model CDL SF z kutą, ryflowaną lufą ze "
"stali nierdzewnej 416, gwintowaną w komorze zamkowej i z zagłębioną główką "
"zamka. Posiada szachownicę z orzecha włoskiego i poduszkę sprężynującą w "
"celu zmniejszenia odczuwalnego odrzutu."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid "M2010 ESR"
msgid_plural "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[0] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[1] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[2] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[3] "M2010 ESR"

#. ~ Description of gun "M2010 ESR"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"A bolt-action, box-magazine-fed sniper rifle chambered in the powerful .300 "
"Winchester Magnum round.  The M2010 had completely replaced the M24 rifle "
"series by 2017."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid "Weatherby Mark V"
msgid_plural "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[0] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[1] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[2] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[3] "Weatherby Mark V"

#. ~ Description of gun "Weatherby Mark V"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"The Weatherby Mark V is one of the world's finest bolt-action rifles.  "
"Designed in 1955 by Roy Weatherby and Fred Jennie, it has a strong action "
"designed to safely fire high-pressure cartridges.  These rifles were "
"presented to celebrities as part of a marketing campaign."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid "Winchester Model 70"
msgid_plural "Winchester Model 70"
msgstr[0] "Winchester Model 70"
msgstr[1] "Winchester Model 70"
msgstr[2] "Winchester Model 70"
msgstr[3] "Winchester Model 70"

#. ~ Description of gun "Winchester Model 70"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"The Winchester Model 70 is a bolt-action sporting rifle.  It has an iconic "
"place in American sporting culture and has been held in high regard by "
"shooters since it was introduced in 1936."
msgstr ""
"Winchester Model 70 to sportowy karabin z czterotaktowym zamkiem. To ikona "
"amerykańskiej kultury sportowej i znalazł uznanie w oczach strzelców od "
"kiedy został wprowadzony w 1936 r."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Browning BLR"
msgid_plural "Browning BLR"
msgstr[0] "Browning BLR"
msgstr[1] "Browning BLR"
msgstr[2] "Browning BLR"
msgstr[3] "Browning BLR"

#. ~ Description of gun "Browning BLR"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A highly accurate lever-action hunting rifle chambered for the powerful "
".30-06 round.  Notable for using a detachable magazine instead of a "
"traditional tube."
msgstr ""
"Bardzo celny sztucer z dwutaktowym zamkiem mieszczący w lufie silne naboje "
".30-60. Godny uwagi na wymienny magazynek w miejscu tradycyjnej tuby."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "M1 Garand"
msgid_plural "M1 Garands"
msgstr[0] "M1 Garand"
msgstr[1] "M1 Garand"
msgstr[2] "M1 Garand"
msgstr[3] "M1 Garand"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1 Garand"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic .30-06 battle rifle, developed to replace the M1903 "
"Springfield.  It didn't completely supplant the older bolt-action until "
"after World War II."
msgstr ""
"Samopowtarzalny karabin kalibru .30-06, zaprojektowany w celu zastąpienia "
"karabinu M1903 Springfield. Nie wyparł do końca starszego karabinu przed "
"końcem drugiej wojny światowej."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "M1903 Springfield"
msgid_plural "M1903 Springfields"
msgstr[0] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[1] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[2] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[3] "M1903 Springfield"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1903 Springfield"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A powerful military rifle chambered in .30-06, developed to replace the US "
"Army's older Krag rifle.  It served as the main American rifle in World War "
"I, was used alongside the M1 Garand in World War II, and was used as a "
"sniper rifle as late as the Vietnam War."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Browning Automatic Rifle"
msgid_plural "Browning Automatic Rifles"
msgstr[0] "BAR"
msgstr[1] "BAR"
msgstr[2] "BAR"
msgstr[3] "BAR"

#. ~ Description of gun "Browning Automatic Rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"Designed near the end of World War I, the BAR provided fire support for the "
"US Army from World War II all the way to the Vietnam War.  Too much "
"firepower to serve as a battle rifle, but not enough to be an ideal light "
"machine gun, it still found a niche on the battlefield."
msgstr ""
"Opracowany przy końcu I wojny światowej, BAR - karabin automatyczny "
"browninga - zapewniał wsparcie ogniowe dla amerykańskiej armii od II wojny "
"światowej aż po wojnę wietnamską. Zbyt wielka siła ognia jak na karabinek "
"automatyczny, lecz zbyt mała jak na idealny lekki karabin maszynowy, lecz "
"pomimo tego znalazł swoją niszę na polu bitwy."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[0] "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[1] "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[2] "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[3] "Remington 700 .30-06"

#. ~ Description of gun "Remington 700 .30-06"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A very popular and durable hunting or sniping rifle.  Popular among SWAT and"
" US Marine snipers.  Highly damaging, but perhaps not as accurate as the "
"competing Browning BLR."
msgstr ""
"Bardzo popularny i wytrzymały karabin myśliwski lub snajperski. Popularny w "
"oddziałach SWAT i snajperów marines. Zadaje duże obrażenia, ale być może nie"
" tak celny jak konkurencyjny Browning BLR."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid "Remington ACR .300BLK"
msgid_plural "Remington ACR .300BLKs"
msgstr[0] "Remington ACR .300BLK"
msgstr[1] "Remington ACR .300BLK"
msgstr[2] "Remington ACR .300BLK"
msgstr[3] "Remington ACR .300BLK"

#. ~ Description of gun "Remington ACR .300BLK"
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid ""
"This carbine was developed for military use in the early 21st century.  It "
"is damaging and accurate, though its rate of fire is a bit slower than "
"competing carbines.  This version is chambered for the .300 AAC Blackout "
"round."
msgstr ""
"Karabinek ten został opracowany do użytku wojskowego na początku XXI wieku. "
"Jest wytrzymały i celny, choć jego szybkostrzelność jest nieco wolniejsza "
"niż konkurencyjnych karabinków. Ta wersja jest na amunicję .300 AAC "
"Blackout."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
msgid_plural "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLKs"
msgstr[0] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
msgstr[1] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
msgstr[2] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
msgstr[3] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"

#. ~ Description of gun "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid ""
"The IWI Tavor X95 (also called Micro-Tavor or MTAR) is an Israeli bullpup "
"assault rifle designed and produced by Israel Weapon Industries.  This is "
"the civilian version chambered for .300 AAC Blackout."
msgstr ""
"IWI Tavor X95 (zwany również Micro-Tavor lub MTAR) to izraelski bezkolbowy "
"karabin automatyczny zaprojektowany i produkowany przez Israel Weapon "
"Industries. Jest to wersja cywilna na nabój .300 AAC Blackout."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgid_plural "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"
msgstr[0] "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgstr[1] "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgstr[2] "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgstr[3] "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid ""
"This is a short-barreled, gas-operated rifle, with a 5.5 inch barrel, built-"
"in thin folding stock, and full rail mount on the upper receiver.  This "
"particular one is a select-fire military version."
msgstr ""
"Jest to karabin o krótkiej lufie, z gazowym mechanizmem, z 5,5-calową lufą, "
"wbudowaną cienką, składaną kolbą i pełną szyną montażową na górnej części "
"korpusu. Ten konkretny egzemplarz to wojskowa wersja z selektywnym trybem "
"ognia."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "FN FAL"
msgid_plural "FN FAL"
msgstr[0] "FN FAL"
msgstr[1] "FN FAL"
msgstr[2] "FN FAL"
msgstr[3] "FN FAL"

#. ~ Description of gun "FN FAL"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"Originally designed during the Cold War, the FN FAL is probably the most "
"successful battle rifle ever designed.  Even though often labeled as "
"obsolete, its high rate of fire and powerful ammunition make it perfectly "
"capable of holding its ground against modern competitors."
msgstr ""
"Pierwotnie opracowany w czasie zimnej wojny, FN FAL to prawdopodobnie "
"najbardziej udany karabin automatyczny. Nawet mimo tego, że często zwany "
"przestarzałym, jego szybkostrzelność i silna amunicja czyni go nadal "
"sprawnym konkurentem współczesnych broni."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "H&K G3"
msgid_plural "H&K G3"
msgstr[0] "H&K G3"
msgstr[1] "H&K G3"
msgstr[2] "H&K G3"
msgstr[3] "H&K G3"

#. ~ Description of gun "H&K G3"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"An early battle rifle developed after the end of WWII.  The G3 is designed "
"to unload large amounts of deadly ammunition, but it is less suitable over "
"long ranges."
msgstr ""
"Wczesny karabin automatyczny opracowany po II wojnie światowej. G3 "
"opracowano dla szybkostrzelności, ale jest mniej użyteczny do walki na "
"daleki dystans."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M134D-H Minigun"
msgid_plural "M134D-H Miniguns"
msgstr[0] "M134D-H Minigun"
msgstr[1] "M134D-H Minigun"
msgstr[2] "M134D-H Minigun"
msgstr[3] "M134D-H Minigun"

#. ~ Description of gun "M134D-H Minigun"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M134D-H Minigun is a (relatively) lightweight heavy rotary machine gun."
"  Its six barrels are rotated by an electric motor, powered by UPS or "
"vehicle.  If you could find enough ammo for it, it would become a "
"devastating weapon.  It must be mounted on a vehicle before use."
msgstr ""
"M134D-H Minigun to relatywnie lekki ciężki obrotowy karabin maszynowy. Jego "
"sześć luf obraca silnik elektryczny, zasilany z UPS-a lub pojazdu. Gdyby "
"znaleźć do niego wystarczająco dużo amunicji, stał by się niszczycielską "
"bronią. Musi być przed użyciem zamontowany na pojeździe."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "M134D-H Minigun"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "low auto"
msgstr "wolny auto."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "M134D-H Minigun"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "CMES laser cannon"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json data/json/items/gun/ups.json
msgid "high auto"
msgstr "szybki auto."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M14 EBR-RI"
msgid_plural "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[0] "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[1] "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[2] "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[3] "M14 EBR-RI"

#. ~ Description of gun "M14 EBR-RI"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A highly modified version of the M14 rifle designed to cover both CQB and "
"designated marksman roles.  A very powerful and versatile rifle, if somewhat"
" heavy."
msgstr ""
"Znacznie zmodyfikowana wersja karabinu M14 opracowana do łączenia roli "
"karabinku do walki w zamkniętych przestrzeniach i karabinu snajperskiego. "
"Bardzo mocny i wszechstronny karabin, choć ciężki."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M1A"
msgid_plural "M1A"
msgstr[0] "M1A"
msgstr[1] "M1A"
msgstr[2] "M1A"
msgstr[3] "M1A"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1A"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The child of the M1 Garand World War II rifle, the M1A is a semi-automatic "
"variant of the M14, favored for its accuracy and modular use."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M240"
msgid_plural "M240s"
msgstr[0] "M240"
msgstr[1] "M240"
msgstr[2] "M240"
msgstr[3] "M240"

#. ~ Description of gun "M240"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M240 is a medium machine gun used by the US military, replacing the "
"older M60.  Quite inaccurate and difficult to control, the M240 is designed "
"to fire many rounds very quickly."
msgstr ""
"M240 to erkaem używany przez siły zbrojne USA, zastępujący starszy M60. Dość"
" niecelny i ciężki do kontrolowania, jest opracowany dla szybkostrzelności."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M60"
msgid_plural "M60s"
msgstr[0] "M60"
msgstr[1] "M60"
msgstr[2] "M60"
msgstr[3] "M60"

#. ~ Description of gun "M60"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M60 is a general-purpose machine gun developed to replace the "
".30-caliber M1918 and M1919.  Heavy and difficult to handle fired from the "
"shoulder, as most people aren't action-movie heroes."
msgstr ""
"M60 to ogólnego przeznaczenia karabin maszynowy opracowany, by zastąpić "
"używających kalibru .30 M1918 i M1919. Ciężki i trudny w utrzymaniu przy "
"strzelaniu z ramienia, gdyż większość ludzi nie jest herosami z filmów "
"akcji."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M60 Semi Auto"
msgid_plural "M60 Semi Autos"
msgstr[0] "M60 Semi Auto"
msgstr[1] "M60 Semi Auto"
msgstr[2] "M60 Semi Auto"
msgstr[3] "M60 Semi Auto"

#. ~ Description of gun "M60 Semi Auto"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic civilian variant of the M60 machine gun, retaining the "
"ability to be belt fed, an uncommon feature in civilian firearms."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "Savage 111F"
msgid_plural "Savage 111F"
msgstr[0] "Savage 111F"
msgstr[1] "Savage 111F"
msgstr[2] "Savage 111F"
msgstr[3] "Savage 111F"

#. ~ Description of gun "Savage 111F"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A very accurate rifle chambered for the powerful .308 round.  Its very low "
"ammo capacity is offset by its accuracy and near-complete lack of recoil."
msgstr ""
"Bardzo celny karabin na mocną amunicję .308. Jego niska pojemność amunicyjna"
" jest równoważona jego celnością i niemal zupełnym brakiem odrzutu."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "FN SCAR-H"
msgid_plural "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[0] "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[1] "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[2] "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[3] "FN SCAR-H"

#. ~ Description of gun "FN SCAR-H"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A highly accurate and modular battle rifle specially designed for the United"
" States Special Operations Command.  The 'H' in its name stands for heavy, "
"as it uses the powerful .308 round."
msgstr ""
"Bardzo celny modularny karabin automatyczny opracowany dla amerykańskiego "
"dowództwa operacji specjalnych. Litera „H” oznacza ciężki, ponieważ używa "
"silnej amunicji .308."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M24"
msgid_plural "M24"
msgstr[0] "M24"
msgstr[1] "M24"
msgstr[2] "M24"
msgstr[3] "M24"

#. ~ Description of gun "M24"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M24 Sniper is the military and police version of the Remington Model 700"
" rifle, M24 being the model name assigned by the United States Army after "
"adoption as their standard sniper rifle in 1988.  The M24 is referred to as "
"a 'weapon system' because it consists of not only a rifle, but also a "
"detachable telescopic sight and other accessories."
msgstr ""
"Karabin wyborowy M24 jest wojskową i policyjną wersją karabinu Remington "
"model 700. M24 jest modelem nadanym przez armię Stanów Zjednoczonych po "
"wdrożeniu jej jako standardowy karabin wyborowy w roku 1988. M24 jest "
"nazwany „systemem broni” ponieważ zawiera nie tylko karabin, ale także "
"wymienny celownik optyczny i inne akcesoria."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "HK417 A2"
msgid_plural "HK417 A2s"
msgstr[0] "HK417 A2"
msgstr[1] "HK417 A2"
msgstr[2] "HK417 A2"
msgstr[3] "HK417 A2"

#. ~ Description of gun "HK417 A2"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A German battle rifle with a 13\" barrel and telescopic stock.  It is a gas-"
"operated, rotating bolt rifle with a short-stroke piston design similar to "
"that of the G36."
msgstr ""
"Niemiecki karabin automatyczny z 13-calową lufą i teleskopowym magazynkiem. "
"Jest to karabin o mechanizmie gazowym, z obrotowym ryglem i krótkim skokiem "
"tłoka, podobny do tego z G36."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M110A1"
msgid_plural "M110A1s"
msgstr[0] "M110A1"
msgstr[1] "M110A1"
msgstr[2] "M110A1"
msgstr[3] "M110A1"

#. ~ Description of gun "M110A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A derivative of H&K's G28 with an aluminum upper receiver to meet US Army "
"weight requirements.  It is a gas-operated, rotating bolt rifle accurate to "
"1.5 MOA with standard ammunition."
msgstr ""
"Pochodna modelu G28 firmy H&K z aluminiowym górnym korpusem, aby sprostać "
"wymaganiom wagowym armii USA. Jest to karabin z gazowym mechanizmem i "
"obrotowym ryglem, celny do 1,5 MOA przy użyciu standardowej amunicji."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "7.62x51mm AK"
msgid_plural "7.62x51mm AKs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "7.62x51mm AK"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "A civilian AK pattern rifle, chambered in 7.62x51mm NATO."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "7.62x51mm AK"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "PAP M77"
msgid_plural "PAP M77s"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "7.62x51mm AK" of gun "PAP M77"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A Serbian-made AK pattern rifle made by Zastava in 7.62x51mm NATO.  To avoid"
" import restrictions, Zastava USA has added a number of American-made parts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "AR-10"
msgid_plural "AR-10s"
msgstr[0] "AR-10"
msgstr[1] "AR-10"
msgstr[2] "AR-10"
msgstr[3] "AR-10"

#. ~ Description of gun "AR-10"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"Somewhat similar to the later AR-15, the AR-10 is a gas-operated, rotating "
"bolt rifle chambered for 7.62x51mm rounds."
msgstr ""
"Nieco podobny do późniejszego AR-15, AR-10 jest napędzanym mechanizmem "
"gazowym karabinem z obrotowym ryglem, przystosowanym do nabojów 7,62 x 51 "
"mm."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
msgid "M1 carbine"
msgid_plural "M1 carbines"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "M1 carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
msgid ""
"A light rifle developed during the Second World War to provide a less "
"cumbersome weapon for soldiers that didn't need the firepower of the M1 "
