#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/700nx.json
msgid "Elephant gun"
msgid_plural "Elephant guns"
msgstr[0] "broń na słonie"
msgstr[1] "bronie na słonie"
msgstr[2] "broni na słonie"
msgstr[3] "broni na słonie"

#. ~ Description of gun "Elephant gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/700nx.json
msgid ""
"A custom-made single shot rifle specially designed for the hunting of huge "
"game.  You could obviously kill everything with this, EVERYTHING.  If you "
"ever find enough ammo of course."
msgstr ""
"Produkowany na zamówienie karabin zaprojektowany na bardzo grubego zwierza. "
"Możesz z niego zabić dosłownie WSZYSTKO. Jeżeli tylko kiedykolwiek "
"znajdziesz wystarczająco amunicji."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "AKM"
msgid_plural "AKMs"
msgstr[0] "AKM"
msgstr[1] "AKM"
msgstr[2] "AKM"
msgstr[3] "AKM"

#. ~ Description of gun "AKM"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"One of the most recognizable assault rifles ever made, the AKM is renowned "
"for its durability even under the worst conditions."
msgstr ""
"Jeden z najbardziej rozpoznawalnych karabinków automatycznych wszech czasów."
" AKM to broń znana z niezawodności nawet w najgorszych warunkach polowych."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Beretta ARX-160"
msgid_plural "Beretta ARX-160"
msgstr[0] "Beretta ARX-160"
msgstr[1] "Beretta ARX-160"
msgstr[2] "Beretta ARX-160"
msgstr[3] "Beretta ARX-160"

#. ~ Description of gun "Beretta ARX-160"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"The Beretta ARX-160 was a Phase II contender in the United States Army "
"Individual Carbine competition to replace the M4 carbine.  It failed to "
"replace it, but it is widely used by military all around the world.  This "
"version is chambered for 7.62x39mm."
msgstr ""
"Beretta ARX-160 to pretendent drugiej fazy konkursu armii USA na "
"indywidualny karabinek mający zastąpić M4. Nie udało mu się go zastąpić, ale"
" jest stosowany przez wojska na świecie. Ta wersja jest ma kaliber 7,62 x 39"
" mm."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "SKS"
msgid_plural "SKSs"
msgstr[0] "SKS"
msgstr[1] "SKS"
msgstr[2] "SKS"
msgstr[3] "SKS"

#. ~ Description of gun "SKS"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"Developed by the Soviets in 1945, this rifle was quickly replaced by the "
"full-auto AK-47.  However, due to its superb accuracy, low recoil, and "
"deployable integrated bayonet, this gun maintains immense popularity."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "AK-47"
msgid_plural "AK-47s"
msgstr[0] "AK-47"
msgstr[1] "AK-47"
msgstr[2] "AK-47"
msgstr[3] "AK-47"

#. ~ Description of gun "AK-47"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"Civilian-legal clones of the iconic Kalashnikov, like this one, were "
"manufactured and imported by many different firms.  Even without full-auto "
"function, their solid firepower and reliability in harsh conditions make "
"them valuable weapons in this new world."
msgstr ""
"Legalne cywilne klony kultowego Kałasznikowa, takie jak ten, były "
"produkowane i importowane przez wiele różnych firm. Nawet bez funkcji "
"strzelania serią, ich solidna siła ognia i niezawodność w trudnych warunkach"
" czynią je wartościową bronią w nowym świecie."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Mini Draco"
msgid_plural "Mini Dracos"
msgstr[0] "Mini Draco"
msgstr[1] "Mini Draco"
msgstr[2] "Mini Draco"
msgstr[3] "Mini Draco"

#. ~ Description of gun "Mini Draco"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"Essentially a semi-auto AK with a short barrel and no stock, this unwieldy "
"\"pistol\" has seen some popularity with civilian shooters and gangbangers "
"alike."
msgstr ""
"Ten nieporęczny „pistolet”, będący w zasadzie półautomatycznym AK z krótką "
"lufą i bez kolby, zyskał popularność zarówno wśród cywilnych strzelców, jak "
"i gangsterów."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Mk47 Mutant"
msgid_plural "Mk47 Mutants"
msgstr[0] "Mk47 Mutant"
msgstr[1] "Mk47 Mutant"
msgstr[2] "Mk47 Mutant"
msgstr[3] "Mk47 Mutant"

#. ~ Description of gun "Mk47 Mutant"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"The CMMG Mk47 Mutant is an American rifle, natively chambered for 7.62x39mm "
"ammo.  Features a characteristic free-floating handguard, with a similar "
"action mechanism to the AR-15, repurposed for the bigger, more potent ammo."
msgstr ""
"CMMG Mk47 Mutant jest Amerykańskim karabinem, natywnie przystosowany do "
"amunicji 7,62 x 39 mm. Cechuje się charakterystycznym pływającym uchwytem, z"
" podobnym mechanizmem spustowym jak w AR-15, przerobionym do większej, "
"skuteczniejszej amunicji."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "vz. 58 combat rifle"
msgid_plural "vz. 58 combat rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "vz. 58 combat rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"A Cold War-era Czechoslovak assault rifle, likely constructed stateside from"
" a pre-1986 imported parts kit or brought back from a third world war zone."
"  Externally similar to the AK family of rifles, this weapon nevertheless "
"only shares the former’s 7.62x39mm chambering.  Featuring no interchangeable"
" parts with its Russian doppelganger, this firearm makes use of a completely"
" different internal operating system, is far more svelte than its other "
"Warsaw Pact counterparts, and feeds from proprietary box magazines."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "vz. 58 combat rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Samopal vz. 58 P"
msgid_plural "Samopal vz. 58 Ps"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "vz. 58 combat rifle" of gun "Samopal vz. 58 P"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"This lightweight and relatively svelte Cold War assault rifle was originally"
" developed for use by the Czechoslovak army, in place of the various "
"licensed Kalashnikov rifles which were then prevalent around eastern Europe."
"  Bearing more than a passing resemblance to the AK-47, this weapon "
"nevertheless features a completely different array of internals and "
"possesses no interchangeable parts with its Russian counterpart.  Making use"
" of proprietary magazines and a 15.4 inch barrel, the vz. 58 was regarded by"
" some to be the Kalashnikov’s lesser-known superior.  Likely reconstructed "
"from a pre-1986 imported parts kit, or brought back from a third world war "
"zone, this particular weapon features a removable wood impregnated plastic "
"buttstock and a 'P' suffixed designation, which both mark it as an original "
"infantry model."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "vz. 58 combat rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Samopal VZ 58 V"
msgid_plural "Samopal VZ 58 Vs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "vz. 58 combat rifle" of gun "Samopal VZ 58 V"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"This lightweight and relatively svelte Cold War assault rifle was originally"
" developed for use by the Czechoslovak army, in place of the various "
"licensed Kalashnikov rifles which were then prevalent around eastern Europe."
"  Bearing more than a passing resemblance to the AK-47, this weapon "
"nevertheless features a completely different array of internals and "
"possesses no interchangeable parts with its Russian counterpart.  Making use"
" of proprietary magazines and a 15.4 inch barrel, the vz. 58 was regarded by"
" some to be the Kalashnikov’s lesser-known superior.  Likely reconstructed "
"from a pre-1986 imported parts kit, or brought back from a third world war "
"zone, this particular weapon features a removable side-folding buttstock and"
" a 'V' suffixed designation, which both mark it as an original airborne or "
"crew issued model."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "vz. 58 tactical rifle"
msgid_plural "vz. 58 tactical rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "vz. 58 tactical rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"Inspired and built primarily from older Czechoslovak military combat rifles,"
" this weapon bears an uncanny resemblance to the Kalashnikov despite sharing"
" no components with it, including magazines.  Chambering the Soviet "
"7.62x39mm cartridge and featuring an American produced folding buttstock, "
"receiver, and barrel in order to comply with US importation laws, the weapon"
" is equipped with a side mounted rail assembly as well as a detachable "
"muzzle brake.  Despite the firearm’s Cold War design being nearly 80 years "
"old, this modern iteration makes for a relatively portable and serviceable "
"cataclysmic problem solver."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "vz. 58 tactical rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "vz. 58 Tactical Sporter"
msgid_plural "vz. 58 Tactical Sporters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "vz. 58 tactical rifle" of gun "vz. 58 Tactical
#. Sporter"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"A modern semi-automatic clone of the Czechoslovak-produced vz. 58 assault "
"rifle, chambered in the Soviet 7.62x39mm cartridge.  Built off of surplus "
"vz. 58 parts, the rifle makes use of additional American made components "
"such as the receiver, barrel, and buttstock to comply with US importation "
"laws.  Featuring an extended 16 inch barrel, an M4 style stock adapter and "
"tube, and an integrated side rail for optics mounting, this Cold War rifle "
"makes for a relatively handy post-apocalyptic companion."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin carbine"
msgid_plural "Mosin carbines"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Mosin carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"A later produced and substantially shortened version of Imperial Russia’s "
"original service rifle, this variant of the Mosin features a notably more "
"compact barrel and an integral side-folding bayonet.  Produced during the "
"latter days of the Second World War for the Soviet Union, the weapon "
"exhibits less overall stopping power than its full-length older brother "
"thanks to the former’s stubbier barrel.  Despite the arm being somewhat "
"weaker than its forefather, the 7.62x54mm round that it chambers still packs"
" a hefty punch, whilst its smaller size helps to make the weapon wieldier."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Mosin carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin-Nagant M44"
msgid_plural "Mosin-Nagant M44"
msgstr[0] "karabin Mosina wz. 1944"
msgstr[1] "karabiny Mosina wz. 1944"
msgstr[2] "karabinów Mosina wz. 1944"
